===================================================
    
1-1. CHAR/VARCHAR + CHAR/VARCHAR => string concatenation     

===================================================
cast('2' as varchar)+ cast('1' as varchar)    typeof( cast('2' as varchar)+ cast('1' as varchar))    
21     character varying (1073741823)     

===================================================
cast('2' as char(1))+ cast('1' as char(1))    typeof( cast('2' as char(1))+ cast('1' as char(1)))    
21     character varying (2)     

===================================================
    
1-2. CHAR/VARCHAR with -, *, / => DOUBLE (implicit conversion)     

===================================================
cast('2' as char(1))- cast('1' as char(1))    typeof( cast('2' as char(1))- cast('1' as char(1)))    
1.0     double     

===================================================
cast('2' as char(1))* cast('1' as char(1))    typeof( cast('2' as char(1))* cast('1' as char(1)))    
2.0     double     

===================================================
cast('2' as char(1))/ cast('1' as char(1))    typeof( cast('2' as char(1))/ cast('1' as char(1)))    
2.0     double     

===================================================
cast('2' as varchar)- cast('1' as varchar)    typeof( cast('2' as varchar)- cast('1' as varchar))    
1.0     double     

===================================================
cast('2' as varchar)* cast('1' as varchar)    typeof( cast('2' as varchar)* cast('1' as varchar))    
2.0     double     

===================================================
cast('2' as varchar)/ cast('1' as varchar)    typeof( cast('2' as varchar)/ cast('1' as varchar))    
2.0     double     

===================================================
    
1-3. VARCHAR + integer types (SHORT/INT/BIGINT) => DOUBLE     

===================================================
cast('1' as varchar)+ cast(2 as smallint)    typeof( cast('1' as varchar)+ cast(2 as smallint))    
3.0     double     

===================================================
cast('1' as varchar)+ cast(2 as integer)    typeof( cast('1' as varchar)+ cast(2 as integer))    
3.0     double     

===================================================
cast('1' as varchar)+ cast(2 as bigint)    typeof( cast('1' as varchar)+ cast(2 as bigint))    
3.0     double     

===================================================
    
1-4. VARCHAR + Fixed NUMERIC => DOUBLE     

===================================================
cast('1' as varchar)+ cast(2 as numeric(1,0))    typeof( cast('1' as varchar)+ cast(2 as numeric(1,0)))    
3.0     double     

===================================================
    
1-5. VARCHAR + Float NUMERIC => DOUBLE     

===================================================
cast('1' as varchar)+ cast(2 as numeric)    typeof( cast('1' as varchar)+ cast(2 as numeric))    
3.0     double     

===================================================
    
1-6. VARCHAR + FLOAT/DOUBLE => DOUBLE     

===================================================
cast('1' as varchar)+ cast(2.1 as float)    typeof( cast('1' as varchar)+ cast(2.1 as float))    
3.099999905     double     

===================================================
cast('1' as varchar)+ cast(2.1 as double)    typeof( cast('1' as varchar)+ cast(2.1 as double))    
3.1     double     

===================================================
    
1-7. High-precision numeric string collapses to DOUBLE (precision loss)     

===================================================
cast('0.12345678901234567890123456789012345678' as varchar)+ cast(0 as numeric)    typeof( cast('0.12345678901234567890123456789012345678' as varchar)+ cast(0 as numeric))    
0.123456789     double     

===================================================
    
1-8. Decimal and scientific-notation strings convert to DOUBLE     

===================================================
cast('2.5' as varchar)- cast('1' as varchar)    typeof( cast('2.5' as varchar)- cast('1' as varchar))    
1.5     double     

===================================================
cast('1e3' as varchar)+ cast(0 as integer)    typeof( cast('1e3' as varchar)+ cast(0 as integer))    
1000.0     double     

===================================================
cast('.5' as varchar)* cast('4' as varchar)    typeof( cast('.5' as varchar)* cast('4' as varchar))    
2.0     double     

===================================================
    
1-9. Non-numeric string in arithmetic (error)     

===================================================
Error:-181
